	<BrightnessNormalization_ForMainStars>0.3</BrightnessNormalization_ForMainStars>
	<!-- with the main stars we have the problem that some colors just look brighter than others because they have more energy. for example, white has 3x as much energy (255 red + 255 blue + 255 green) as red (255 red plus a little bit of other stuff). When you set that factor to 1, the full correction is being applied and white stars get 1/3 as much brightess as red strs. When you set the factor to 0, no corretion is being applied. Beware, this parameter behaves in a very non-linear way (in some parts of the range, small changes have huge effects) -->
